@tradition rec-slow-stretch
// W3 (rec writer; lead 18: fields from plans/rec-traditions-plan.html FINAL and the brief; RA owns the format).
// Slow stretch: Sundays 08:00-08:45 from Day 7 (lead 18: moved from 08:30), the float room; Dr. Nandakumar leads a stretch
// at a fifth of a g, 3 to 6 people. Tap to join (the float animation, slower).
k: 493
title: Slow stretch
when: weekly sunday from day 7
at: 08:00-08:45
min: 25
wake: 30
where: 7 room Float room: rec:float
who: nandakumar always, infirmary 30%, everyone 6%
anim: everyone talk
host: nandakumar
from: nandakumar
flag: rec.on

== mail
- Slow stretch tomorrow, {time} in the float room. Dr. Nandakumar leads a gentle stretch at a fifth of a g. Bring water. She'll ask.

== ask
- Slow stretch this morning. It's like stretching in honey. In a good way.
- Coming to slow stretch? Nandakumar says it's good for us. That settles it.

== here
- Slowly. Slower than that.
- Breathe out. Now drink some water.   #funny
- Reach. And float. And reach.

== thanks
- You join the small circle in the float room. Dr. Nandakumar counts, slowly, and your whole back says thank you.   #warm

== chatter
- My back's never been happier than after slow stretch.
- Water break at slow stretch. In low gravity. It went everywhere.   #funny
